# netsurf: antialiased SVG path fills (patch 359)
# Generated 2026-11-01
# Base: seleron/vitabrowser (patch stack through 358)
#
# Path fills were centre-sampled: a pixel drew if its centre was inside
# the shape. Thin shapes -- a 1.5px icon ring, a diagonal at a shallow
# angle -- broke into pixel crumbs, and a 1px bar straddling two columns
# came out one column solid and one empty. Browsers antialias; the Vita
# can (text and rectangles already do).
#
#  - pathfill.c/h: polyfill_aa(), the coverage form of polyfill(). Same
#    shape, rule and clip, but each row reports how much of every pixel
#    the shape covers (0..255 per pixel). Coverage is sampled on
#    POLYFILL_AA_SS=4 sub-scanlines per row, each crossing exactly in x
#    (the canvas rasteriser's method). Rows are reported top to bottom,
#    trimmed to their covered pixels.
#  - plot.c: path fills now use polyfill_aa(). Fully covered runs go
#    through the existing span merger; partial-coverage edge pixels are
#    batched into ONE triangle-list draw per path, the fill colour at
#    that pixel's share of its alpha. Vertices come from vita2d's
#    per-frame pool (VITA_FRAME_POOL, 4 MB), shared with text and
#    rectangles: a path whose edge pixels would leave less than 1 MiB of
#    the pool, that has more than 4096 edge quads, or whose pool
#    allocation fails, falls back to the old centre-sampled look (solid
#    where at least half covered). An allocation failure part-way keeps
#    the rows already made, so no pixel blends twice.
#  - tools: vita2d_pool_free_space() in the sim and plotter stub (the
#    pool answers as the device's 4 MB would, at the size the frontend
#    asked for). Gate line: CSS-svg-aa (file:// snapshot -- a half-
#    covered diagonal pixel and a 1px bar straddling two columns read
#    127 grey, as background and inline SVG).
#
# The sim's fill_triangle also got the GPU's top-left rule (it used to
# include every edge, so a pixel centre on an edge two triangles share
# blended twice -- a translucent 1x1 quad, the AA edge, came out at
# double alpha).
#
# Gate: CSS-svg-aa pixels exact (0,0,0 255,255,255 127,127,127 x5);
# full gate359d exit 0. Scorecard: r84-359-freshref (guardian, bbc,
# hackernews, stackoverflow, rte, fresh Chrome ref at the same time):
# 86.9 vs 87.0 baseline -- no regression. The r81-359 run's 75.7 mean
# is stale-reference drift (ref 20 h old: live news/forum content moved,
# one guardian sim flake with an empty innerText dump), not a code
# change: the five sites recover to baseline on the fresh ref.
